            {
                "box": {
                    "code": "/**\n * ============================================================================\n * @file lp_butterworth.gendsp / lowpasss_highpass.maxpat\n * @title 4th-Order Butterworth Lowpass Filter (24 dB/octave)\n * @author Max Bruckert\n *\n * @description\n * Steep-slope 4th-order (24 dB/octave) lowpass filter consisting of two cascaded\n * 2nd-order biquad stages in Direct Form I. Features exponential parameter\n * smoothing to ensure click-free real-time cutoff modulation.\n *\n * Designed as a high-performance utility crossover and tone filter, ideal for\n * isolating sub-bass frequencies for subwoofer feeds or cutting high frequencies\n * with maximally flat passband response.\n *\n * @inlets\n *   in1 : Audio Input Signal\n *\n * @outlets\n *   out1 : Filtered Lowpass Audio Output (24 dB/oct)\n *\n * @parameters\n *   freq   (10..20000 Hz, def: 80) : Target cutoff frequency in Hz\n *   smooth (0..1000 ms, def: 100)  : Cutoff frequency smoothing time in ms\n * ============================================================================\n */\n\n// 1. PARAMETERS & SMOOTHING\nParam freq(80, min=10, max=20000);  // Target cutoff frequency in Hz\nParam smooth(100, min=0, max=1000); // Cutoff smoothing time in ms\n\n// Smoothing state\nHistory current_freq(80);\n\n// Biquad Stage 1 state\nHistory x1_1(0), x2_1(0), y1_1(0), y2_1(0);\n\n// Biquad Stage 2 state\nHistory x1_2(0), x2_2(0), y1_2(0), y2_2(0);\n\n// --- 1. Cutoff Frequency Smoothing ---\nsmooth_samples = max(1, (smooth * 0.001) * SAMPLERATE);\nalpha_smooth = 1.0 / smooth_samples;\ncurrent_freq = current_freq + alpha_smooth * (freq - current_freq);\n\n// --- 2. 4th-Order Butterworth Lowpass Coefficient Calculation ---\n// Butterworth 4th-order Q factors for cascaded biquad sections:\n// q1 = 1 / (2 * cos(3 * pi / 8)) = 0.541196100146197\n// q2 = 1 / (2 * cos(pi / 8))     = 1.306562964876376\nq1 = 0.541196100146197;\nq2 = 1.306562964876376;\n\nf_clamped = clamp(current_freq, 10.0, SAMPLERATE * 0.49);\n\nw0 = 2.0 * PI * f_clamped / SAMPLERATE;\ncos_w0 = cos(w0);\nsin_w0 = sin(w0);\n\n// Section 1 (12 dB/oct Biquad LPF)\nalpha1 = sin_w0 / (2.0 * q1);\nb0_1 = (1.0 - cos_w0) * 0.5;\nb1_1 = 1.0 - cos_w0;\nb2_1 = (1.0 - cos_w0) * 0.5;\na0_1 = 1.0 + alpha1;\na1_1 = -2.0 * cos_w0;\na2_1 = 1.0 - alpha1;\n\nnb0_1 = b0_1 / a0_1;\nnb1_1 = b1_1 / a0_1;\nnb2_1 = b2_1 / a0_1;\nna1_1 = a1_1 / a0_1;\nna2_1 = a2_1 / a0_1;\n\n// Section 2 (12 dB/oct Biquad LPF)\nalpha2 = sin_w0 / (2.0 * q2);\nb0_2 = (1.0 - cos_w0) * 0.5;\nb1_2 = 1.0 - cos_w0;\nb2_2 = (1.0 - cos_w0) * 0.5;\na0_2 = 1.0 + alpha2;\na1_2 = -2.0 * cos_w0;\na2_2 = 1.0 - alpha2;\n\nnb0_2 = b0_2 / a0_2;\nnb1_2 = b1_2 / a0_2;\nnb2_2 = b2_2 / a0_2;\nna1_2 = a1_2 / a0_2;\nna2_2 = a2_2 / a0_2;\n\n// --- 3. Audio Processing ---\nx0 = in1;\n\n// Biquad 1 (12 dB/oct)\ny0_1 = nb0_1 * x0 + nb1_1 * x1_1 + nb2_1 * x2_1 - na1_1 * y1_1 - na2_1 * y2_1;\nx2_1 = x1_1;\nx1_1 = x0;\ny2_1 = y1_1;\ny1_1 = y0_1;\n\n// Biquad 2 (24 dB/oct total)\ny0_2 = nb0_2 * y0_1 + nb1_2 * x1_2 + nb2_2 * x2_2 - na1_2 * y1_2 - na2_2 * y2_2;\nx2_2 = x1_2;\nx1_2 = y0_1;\ny2_2 = y1_2;\ny1_2 = y0_2;\n\nout1 = y0_2;",
                    "fontface": 0,
                    "fontname": "<Monospaced>",
                    "fontsize": 12.0,
                    "id": "obj-3",
